(5046158, 734662, 30982, '<td valign="top">Oooh - the coveted "no comments during a challenge" award!  I''d bestow it upon you but in my various fits of "I hate this place" I''m afraid I''ve probably misplaced the little gif.  If I find it I will let you know.  As for the shot, undoubtedly not enough motion blur, busy background, etc.  I rather like the crop, and the background is just enough to make me think this isn''t a barber shop, but a school room or backstage somewhere, which adds a bit of interest to this.</td>', 'Oooh - the coveted "no comments during a challenge" award!  I''d bestow it upon you but in my various fits of "I hate this place" I''m afraid I''ve probably misplaced the little gif.  If I find it I will let you know.  As for the shot, undoubtedly not enough motion blur, busy background, etc.  I rather like the crop, and the background is just enough to make me think this isn''t a barber shop, but a school room or backstage somewhere, which adds a bit of interest to this.', '2008-11-05 11:09:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5046159, 732905, 23484, '<td valign="top">I know, by normal DPC standards, where all the photography experts live, this shot is a terrible piece of crap. However, by the Bob Martuch standards, which don''t mean much by the way, this is a very nice image. I really like the way the diagonal slant of the light over powers the image. This would not have been as nice without the processing to accentuate that feel. Good job colleen.</td>', 'I know, by normal DPC standards, where all the photography experts live, this shot is a terrible piece of crap. However, by the Bob Martuch standards, which don''t mean much by the way, this is a very nice image. I really like the way the diagonal slant of the light over powers the image. This would not have been as nice without the processing to accentuate that feel. Good job colleen.', '2008-11-05 11:09:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5046165, 734400, 23484, '<td valign="top">This is a really cool shot.</td>', 'This is a really cool shot.', '2008-11-05 11:10:42.000000', NULL, 0),
